sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Live as Running app / SQLite WAL
    participant Helper as db-backup.mjs
    participant Backup as Host backup files
    participant Restore as New isolated Docker volume
    participant Check as Restored app on a different port
    Helper->>Live: Open existing database read-only
    Live-->>Helper: Online backup API includes committed WAL data
    Helper->>Helper: Integrity check + required tables + SHA-256
    Helper->>Backup: Snapshot + metadata, private file permissions
    Note over Backup: Managed retention: seven daily snapshots + newest predeployment snapshot
    Backup->>Restore: Check metadata, checksum and approved image, refuse existing volume
    Restore->>Restore: Verify SQLite integrity and set UID 1000 ownership
    Restore->>Check: Start separate project / network / port
    Check->>Check: Verify account, session and known ticket
    Note over Live,Check: Original data stays in place. An image rollback and a data restore are different operations.
    Note over Backup,Check: Off-host copying and a production data switch are separate operator actions.
